    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d669">

                <pb facs="0573" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg561"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.61A/2: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-06T21:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1942—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>115. Your 190, February 3, 10 a.m. Department of Interior irrigation expert has
                    been selected and choice of Department of Agriculture expert lies between two
                    officials. It is planned to send Twitchell<anchor n="8a" xml:id="d669-f1"/>
                    <pb facs="0574" n="562" xml:id="pg562"/> as head of this mission, which has
                    received the President’s informal approval. It is hoped that the President will
                    send a letter to Ibn Saud and that you will find it possible to present in
                    person this message, which would offer the Mission as an evidence of good will.
                    For your strictly confidential information, the Army Air Corps is considering
                    the desirability of establishing one or more airfields in Saudi Arabia on the
                    basis of a suitable <hi rendition="#italic">quid pro quo</hi> but has not yet
                    made a decision of principle. You may, therefore, be requested to take this
                    matter up at the time of your visit.</p>
                <p>As soon as these matters take definite form, which should occur in the near
                    future, you will be promptly advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d669-f1" n="8a" xml:id="d669-f1-content">
                <p>Karl S. Twitchell, American mining and hydraulic engineer, long associated with
                    roadbuilding, well-drilling, and development of mining interests in Saudi Arabia
                    as a representative of American and British capital, and for some time the
                    informal agent of King Ibn Saud in the United States in respect of projects for
                    economic development.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
